# ========================================================
# TRANZORA CLOUD DATABASE CONFIGURATION (FOR VERCEL / MULTI-DEVICE)
# ========================================================
# When running locally on your computer, the app stores data
# inside the local `/data` directory automatically (zero setup needed).
#
# When deploying to Vercel so all users/devices share the exact same data:
# 1. On your Vercel project dashboard, go to the "Storage" tab.
# 2. Click "Create Database" -> choose "KV (Upstash Redis)".
# 3. Connect it to your project. Vercel automatically sets:
#    - KV_REST_API_URL
#    - KV_REST_API_TOKEN
#
# (Alternatively, you can get a free Redis database from upstash.com):
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Or using Upstash naming convention:
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
